sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ha09-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In all animals with separate sexes the female is less spirited (less courageous) than the male, except in the bear and the leopard, where the female is the more courageous.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Females are less spirited than males, except in the bear and leopard";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, The History of Animals (Historia Animalium), Book IX, Part 1; translated by D'Arcy Wentworth Thompson, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. IV (1910). Scope: animals with separate sexes, with the bear and leopard as exceptions"
}
